  "body": "## Summary\n\n- Serialize canonical checkout attempts and give each new request its own intent. Replaying an exact existing request preserves old intent keys, references and fingerprints; a changed key cannot start another unresolved charge.\n- Give new PlaceToPay/PayPhone attempts distinct provider references. Keep legacy PayPal create/capture on the same bound intent, with one capture key.\n- Validate PlaceToPay's actual approved transaction amounts, reference, internal ID and reversal evidence. Conflicting, partial, duplicate or refunded results cannot mark an order paid or unlock fallback.\n- Reuse the original Datafast debit-sale attempt when confirming mixing/mastering payments; this status GET is not a new capture.\n- Add integer-overflow protection and real PostgreSQL concurrency/compatibility tests. The test executable is threaded; database lock waits are bounded.\n\n## Dependencies / review order\n\nDraft only. Depends on #334, which depends on #332 and #331.\nReview/merge order: **#331 \u2192 #332 \u2192 #334 \u2192 this PR**. No merge is authorized by this PR.\n\n## Verification\n\nSource commits: `791086c3acfc0bd7f97939c5b99cc8d00432bb15`, `f837056476a8171e2e25a84c3456006aa6362892`.\n\n| Evidence | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cd tdf-hq && stack test --fast` | 2,556 examples passed, zero failures |\n| `sh scripts/test-provider-retry-runtime.sh` | 9 real PostgreSQL tests passed; concurrent connections, synthetic records, no provider calls |\n| Focused web session/resume/hosted-checkout/return tests | 4 suites, 16 tests passed |\n| Catalog discovery and exhaustive audit | Passed; 1,413 files / 1,122 candidates, no unreviewed or stale decisions |\n| Provider sandboxes / staging / live transactions | Not executed; account, contract and credential blockers unchanged |\n| Hosted CI for this PR | Pending GitHub execution; local tests are not presented as hosted evidence |\n\nThe test record also discloses the initial Docker permission refusal, interrupted non-threaded concurrency run, and subsequent fixture/cache-related failures. They were corrected before the passing rerun; no assertion or quality gate was weakened.\n\n## Migration, rollout and risk\n\nNo schema migration, historical backfill, API/OpenAPI change, feature activation or deployment. No frontend/mobile source change or screenshot was needed for this repair.\n\nDo not mix old and new create writers during rollout. Pause creation for the application cutover, retain reconciliation and all historical references, and prefer roll-forward. Strict one-time USD reconciliation rejects unsupported provider flow/amount variants for review. Cancellation remains an unexposed adapter contract; this PR does not add refunds, payouts, recurring mandates or connected-account custody.\n\nFull audit, official sources, test commands, rollback considerations and outstanding implementations:\n`docs/payments/retry-reconciliation-safety-2026-09-14.md`.\n\nThe overall payment-platform objective remains incomplete. Production activation and credentialed provider verification still require the documented human actions.\n",
